server 目录是我们指定服务器函数所在位置的地方，这是 Nitro 喜欢的方式。
The server directory is us specifying where the server functions to find the way Nitro likes are.

473
00:40:20,366 --> 00:40:30,244
通过把这个放在这里，我们能够定义自己的 nitro 函数，而不是在 Tanstack 中定义它们，这有点有趣，因为如果我们回到我之前的计划，
And by putting this here, we are able to define our own nitro functions outside of defining them in Tanstack, which is kind of funny because if we go back to what my previous plan was,

474
00:40:30,574 --> 00:40:36,260
我们几乎重现了很久以前我就提到过想要的那种 V plus Hano 设置。
we've almost recreated the V plus Hano setup that I was talking about wanting way, way back.

475
00:40:36,656 --> 00:40:39,856
但现在，这一切都在 TanStack Start 内部完成了。
But instead, it's all being done inside of Tanstack Start.

476
00:40:40,016 --> 00:40:45,892
与其在框架外部做这些，我们现在在框架内部做，虽然这确实需要不少补丁处理。
Instead of doing this on the outside of the framework, we're doing it inside of the framework, which does admittedly require quite a few hacks.

477
00:40:46,254 --> 00:40:54,564
为了暴露事件辅助函数以便我们能够访问它，而不得不给 TanStack Start 打补丁这一点确实有点烦人。
The fact that we had to patch package Tanstack Start in order to expose the event helper so we'd have access to that is a little annoying.

478
00:40:54,926 --> 00:40:57,412
理想情况下，没人需要这个 get H3 event 之类的东西，
Ideally, nobody would need this get H3 event thing,

479
00:40:58,158 --> 00:41:02,916
但我们确实需要，因为在我们要交付的规模下，我们无法使用 TanStack 的路由。
but we do, because we couldn't use the Tanstack routes at the scale we're shipping.

480
00:41:04,230 --> 00:41:12,736
而且我没意识到为了处理我们的分析代理还需要做这么多乱七八糟的事情，因为它在代理时会使用错误的内容编码。
And I didn't realize how many other random hellish things we had to do for handling our analytics proxy because it would use the wrong content encoding when we proxy.

481
00:41:12,816 --> 00:41:19,936
天哪，这些琐碎的小问题太多了。就像有人告诉你我们的 Next.js 方案全是各种补丁，我们可以换掉它，把那些补丁都去掉。
God, there's so many of these little things. Like anybody telling you that our next JS solution was a bunch of hacks and we could just move off it and get rid of the hacks.

482
00:41:20,622 --> 00:41:25,508
不过，任何足够大的应用，在各个方面总会有一些权宜之计。
Now, Any large enough application will have hacks in every direction always.

483
00:41:25,838 --> 00:41:30,276
我们用一套更危险的方案换成了一套整体上没那么危险的方案。
We traded one set that were scarier for a set that is overall less scary.

484
00:41:30,670 --> 00:41:38,564
但仍有一些情况，比如因为内容编码可能会出问题，我们不得不从公共目录提供这个文件，而不是通过重定向来提供。
But there are still things like this, where we have to serve this file from our public directory instead of serving it through this redirect because of the way the content encoding would break.

485
00:41:39,278 --> 00:41:42,596
现在到了这个最大时长 799 的问题。
And now we get to this max duration 799 thing.

486
00:41:43,022 --> 00:41:44,900
很有可能你看到这个时在想，
There's a good chance you're looking at that and thinking,

487
00:41:45,550 --> 00:41:46,436
“这到底是个什么鬼？”
what the fuck is that?

488
00:41:47,022 --> 00:41:48,016
这是一个非常好的问题。
That's a really good question.

489
00:41:48,366 --> 00:41:56,416
在我们构建大部分 T3 chat 时，请求在 VerseL 服务器上被强制中断前的最大运行时间是 800 秒。
At the time we built most of T3 chat, the maximum duration for how long a request could be in flight for on a VerseL server before it is killed was 800 seconds.

490
00:41:56,750 --> 00:42:01,252
所以如果你有一个需要 900 秒的 AI 生成任务，它会在到点前被切断。
So if you have an AI generation that takes 900 seconds, it's going to get cut off before then.

491
00:42:01,582 --> 00:42:04,772
默认值是 300，但实际的硬上限是 800。
The default is 300, but the actual hard max is 800.

492
00:42:05,262 --> 00:42:06,724
那我们为什么要选 799？
So why do we pick 799?

493
00:42:07,296 --> 00:42:09,988
答案没你想象的那么简单。
Not as simple to answer as you might hope.

494
00:42:10,416 --> 00:42:17,536
回到 Next.js 版本，你会注意到我把这个放在了 API chat 路由上。
Going back to the next JS version, you will notice that I put this on the API chat route.

495
00:42:18,222 --> 00:42:19,684
就是那个最大时长 799。
The max duration 799.

496
00:42:20,462 --> 00:42:22,032
原因就在这里。
The reason I describe here.

497
00:42:22,286 --> 00:42:26,032
这能让 API chat 路由从流式计算的捆绑中解脱出来。
This breaks out the API chat route from being bundled in fluid compute.

498
00:42:26,286 --> 00:42:29,552
其他函数处理得更快，不会干扰到这个特定路由的运行。
Other functions resolve faster and get in the way of paralyzing this particular route.

499
00:42:29,774 --> 00:42:31,632
这是一个由 Malta 建议的补丁。
This is a hack that was suggested by Malta.

500
00:42:31,952 --> 00:42:42,432
流式计算运作的一个重要部分是，它是一种允许一个 Node 或者一个运行 Node 的 Lambda 实例同时处理多个请求的策略。
One of the important pieces of how fluid compute works is it is a strategy to allow for many requests to be resolved by one node or one instance of Lambda running node at the same time.

501
00:42:42,670 --> 00:42:50,820
通常 Lambda 的工作方式是：请求进来，被处理，然后该 Lambda 处理完上一个请求后再接下一个，但它一次只能处理一个。
Normally the way Lambda works is a request comes in, it gets resolved, and then that Lambda takes the next request once it's done with the previous one, but it only does one at a time.

502
00:42:51,278 --> 00:42:59,792
所以如果你的请求逻辑在花费大量时间等待，那个 Node 就只是在那儿闲置，什么也不干，直到下一个……
So if your request logic is spending a lot of time waiting, that node is just sitting there doing nothing until the next like

503
00:43:00,270 --> 00:43:02,112
……该处理的片段进来。
piece of whatever it's supposed to do comes in.

504
00:43:02,350 --> 00:43:09,952
如果你正在进行 AI 生成并调用 OpenAI 的 ChatGPT API，每当你没拿到新 token 时，你就在那儿闲置。
So if you're doing an AI generation and you're hitting the open AI API for Chat GPT, whenever you're not getting a new token, you're sitting there doing nothing.

505
00:43:10,318 --> 00:43:18,832
这就是流式计算很牛的地方，因为它能让你利用那些原本就在闲置、等待从 API 获取下一块数据的计算资源。
This is why fluid compute is awesome, because it lets you reuse that less used compute that would just be sitting there doing nothing, waiting for the next like chunk to come from the API.

506
00:43:19,054 --> 00:43:21,188
你可以用这些计算资源去处理其他的请求。
And you can use that compute to resolve other requests.

507
00:43:21,550 --> 00:43:27,712
这样五个用户可以同时发起请求，而且所有请求都能同时处理。
So five people can be requesting at the same time, and all of that is going through at once.

508
00:43:28,078 --> 00:43:33,540
非常棒。这能让你省下很多钱，并更好地利用你的服务器。
Super nice. Let's you pay way less money and take much more advantage of your servers.

509
00:43:33,902 --> 00:43:36,672
当你的请求只需要 100 毫秒时，这并不重要。
When your request only took like 100 milliseconds, this didn't matter.

510
00:43:36,942 --> 00:43:40,036
现在既然请求可能需要 800 秒，这就变得非常重要了。
Now that the request can take 800 seconds, it matters a lot more.

511
00:43:40,430 --> 00:43:42,532
那为什么我在这里选了 799？
So why did I pick 799 here?

512
00:43:42,912 --> 00:43:45,572
因为其他所有路由都设成了 800。
Because every other route was set to 800.

513
00:43:45,902 --> 00:43:53,632
如果你有两个具有不同最大持续时间的路由，流式计算的配置和部署方式就会
If you have two different routes that have different max durations, the way that Fluid Compute is provisioned and deployed would

514
00:43:53,632 --> 00:44:02,756
允许所有共享相同最大持续时的请求被合并处理，而那些没有共同最大持续时的请求则会被独立拆分出来。
allow for all of the ones that share a max duration to be served together and the ones that don't have a shared max duration to be broken off on their own.

515
00:44:03,118 --> 00:44:13,188
所以实际上，这保证了所有的 API/chat 请求都会进入同一组 Lambda，而其他所有请求则进入另一组。
So effectively, this guarantees all API slash chat requests go to the same set of lambdas and all other requests go to a different set.

516
00:44:13,518 --> 00:44:21,220
这一秒的差异设置能把包拆分开，让它们独立存在，不同的路由会命中不同的机器。
The setting of this one second difference breaks out the bundles so that they are separate and different routes are hitting different boxes.

517
00:44:21,454 --> 00:44:28,900
这非常棒，因为它意味着在同一个 Lambda 上进行聊天去重和处理所有聊天请求可以更好地扩展。
This was great because it meant that the chat deduping and handling all of the chat requests on one lambda could scale way better.

518
00:44:29,166 --> 00:44:33,508
因为现在，假设一下，其中一台机器可以处理一千个请求。
Because now, like let's say hypothetically, one of these boxes can handle a thousand requests.

519
00:44:34,112 --> 00:44:44,484
如果其中三分之一是耗时高达 800 秒的聊天请求，而剩下的全是耗时仅 50 毫秒的 TRPC 调用，那就不是流式计算的最优利用方式。
If a third of them are chat requests that take 800 seconds up to, and the rest are all TRPC calls that take 50 milliseconds, that is not an optimal use of fluid compute.

520
00:44:44,752 --> 00:44:54,352
理想情况下，能够处理长请求的机器应该处理大量的此类请求，而不应该被那些 I/O 更多、但耗时更短的任务占用掉可用名额。
Ideally, the box that can handle long requests is handling a lot of them, and its slots for how many requests it can handle aren't being wasted by something that does more I.O.

521
00:44:54,512 --> 00:44:57,188
每秒钟的处理量更高，且耗时更少。
per second and is going for way fewer seconds.

522
00:44:57,550 --> 00:45:04,452
有了这个微小的提示，流式计算的路由层就更容易知道如何进行分发了。
It's way easier for the fluid compute like routing layer to know how to route things with this little hint.

523
00:45:05,358 --> 00:45:13,712
而我们现在基本上失去了这一点，因为据我所知，在这里设置最大持续时间会将所有的 API 都打包到一起。
And we have basically lost that here because as far as I understand, putting this max duration here is making all of our APIs bundled under that.

524
00:45:13,838 --> 00:45:22,912
所以我们不再有专门拆分出来的 chat 端点，但我们确实把 API 端点与 TanStack Start 的端点分开处理了。
So we no longer have the chat endpoint split off from the other API endpoints, but we do have the API endpoints split off separately from the TanStack start ones,

525
00:45:22,992 --> 00:45:30,948
这目前是个足够好的解决方案，因为我们已经大幅减少了这些 API 调用。现在大部分内容都通过 Convex 和 chat 端点进行处理。
which is a good enough solution for now because we've really reduced the number of those API calls that happened. Most of everything now goes through convex and the chat endpoint.

526
00:45:31,152 --> 00:45:38,912
即便如此，如果我们还能只针对 chat 修改持续时间，让它单独打包并最大化流式计算的利用率，那就更好了。
That said, it would be nice if we could still change the duration on just chat so it would be bundled separately and maximize our fluid compute usage.

527
00:45:39,150 --> 00:45:41,924
让我去查一下我们目前的流式计算使用情况。
Let me actually go check how our fluid compute use is right now.

528
00:45:42,414 --> 00:45:50,660
我想看看这个变化对我们流式计算利用率的影响，但是他们把我在 Verse L 里通常查看的仪表盘删了，所以我没法展示给你们看。
I wanted to see how this change affected our fluid compute utilization, but uh they got rid of the dashboard that I would normally check that in in Verse L, so I can't show you.

529
00:45:51,374 --> 00:45:51,972
真烦人。
Annoying.

530
00:45:52,430 --> 00:45:54,020
现在是最后一部分
So now for the last piece

531
00:45:54,766 --> 00:45:55,524
服务端渲染。
SSR.

532
00:45:56,366 --> 00:46:02,564
判断我们现在有 服务端渲染 最简单的方法是，当你打开一个无痕标签页并加载时，你会看到骨架屏
The easiest way to know that we have SSR now is when you go to an INCOG tab and load, you'll see the skeleton

533
00:46:03,662 --> 00:46:04,832
我不怎么喜欢这个。
that I don't like very much.

534
00:46:06,542 --> 00:46:11,172
看底部那里显示登录状态的地方，然后它消失了变成登录按钮。
See the bottom there where it shows the login state and then it vanishes and becomes the login button.

535
00:46:11,790 --> 00:46:14,372
看这里的侧边栏，这里有虚假的空聊天记录。
See the sidebar here where it has the fake empty chats.

536
00:46:15,374 --> 00:46:22,788
这是因为我们现在渲染的是模板，然后在服务器完成或客户端处理完后填入内容，针对不同的路由。
That's all because we are now rendering a template and then filling in the pieces once the server finishes them or the client does for different routes.

537
00:46:23,118 --> 00:46:31,812
对于某些特定的内容，比如你第一次加载某个特定聊天时，我们在服务器端进行渲染，以便在你本地开始加载页面之前尽可能获取到更多数据。
And for certain things, like when you load a specific chat for the first time, we render it on the server to get as much of the data there as possible before you start loading the page on your side.

538
00:46:32,142 --> 00:46:34,352
从理论上讲，这应该非常出色。
Hypothetically, this should be really good.

539
00:46:34,670 --> 00:46:35,684
而且在很多方面，它确实很棒。
And in a lot of ways, it is.

540
00:46:36,078 --> 00:46:44,964
比如当我在这里切换页面时，感觉很流畅。而且当我刷新时，加载几乎是瞬间完成的，而且在你操作时能获得更好的聊天历史状态。
Like when I'm navigating around here, it feels good. And when I refresh, it loads pretty much instantly, and you get a better state for your chat history when it happens.

541
00:46:45,550 --> 00:46:52,068
在很多方面它都很出色，但我仍然怀疑服务端渲染到底能给我们带来多少好处。
It is in a lot of ways good, but I am still skeptical of how much we benefit from server rendering at all.

542
00:46:52,494 --> 00:46:54,592
我是团队里最怀疑的人。
I am the most skeptical one on the team.

543
00:46:54,752 --> 00:46:56,644
我不觉得这是必须的。
I don't think this is necessary.

544
00:46:57,232 --> 00:47:04,004
我一直在考虑要不要放弃它。不过，首屏加载能有更好的状态确实很酷。
I am highly considering pulling us off of it. But it is cool that the first load has like a better state overall.

545
00:47:04,558 --> 00:47:09,952
它也有一些坑。比如最初名字加载的方式就不对，我们现在大部分已经修复了。
It has its catches. Like the way that the names load in was not right originally. We've fixed it for the most part.

546
00:47:10,158 --> 00:47:14,820
从服务器端发送更优的有效负载，这确实非常酷。
It is really cool that we're sending down a better payload from the server than we previously were.

547
00:47:15,118 --> 00:47:23,108
但与此同时，我更倾向于用一个 HTML 文件来承载大部分网站内容，然后在合适的地方全部在客户端处理。
But at the same time, I think I would prefer if we had one HTML file serving the majority of our site and just did everything on client side where it made sense to.

548
00:47:23,312 --> 00:47:26,532
不过，我并不是做这些决策的人。
But again, I'm not the one who made these decisions.

549
00:47:26,894 --> 00:47:29,924
我不再是 T3 chat 的技术负责人了。
I'm not really the tech lead for T3 chat anymore.

550
00:47:30,112 --> 00:47:35,872
我得经营公司、做这个频道，还要处理每天必须完成的其他所有事情。
I have to run the company and do this channel and do everything else that I have to do in a given day.

551
00:47:36,110 --> 00:47:39,392
我的团队做出了这些决定，因为我雇佣他们就是为了让他们做出正确的决策。
My team made these decisions because I hired my team to make good decisions.

552
00:47:39,632 --> 00:47:43,012
这是他们想要的决定，我也充分讨论过这个问题。
This is the decision that they wanted, and I have argued it plenty.

553
00:47:43,342 --> 00:47:48,740
他们依然相信这是正确的选择。在团队决定改变之前，我都会继续支持他们。
They are still confident it was the right one. And I will continue to back them until we as a team decide otherwise.

554
00:47:49,102 --> 00:47:58,084
而且至少我们比 Twitch chat 要稳定。挺有意思的，因为我以前还吹牛说 Twitch chat 是我们能够快速构建复杂、高频更新聊天界面的证明。
And at least we're more stable than Twitch chat. It's funny because I've previously bragged that Twitch chat is proof that we know how to do quickly updating, complex chat UIs.

555
00:47:58,414 --> 00:48:00,612
而现在，就在我录制视频的时候，Twitch chat 居然挂了。
And now Twitch chat is down literally as I am filming.

556
00:48:02,030 --> 00:48:05,472
我们离开 Next.js 不是因为 Next.js 不好。
Our move off of Next.js isn't because Next.js is bad.

557
00:48:05,552 --> 00:48:08,676
也不是因为我们对 Tanstack Start 极其兴奋。
It's not because we are super excited about Tanstack start.

558
00:48:08,992 --> 00:48:17,232
而是出于我们在二月份初步规划时就考虑过的原因，即我为了让 Next.js 按我们的要求运行而做的各种折腾并不理想。
It is for the same reasons that it was when we were first planning it back in February, which is that the way I'm hacking Next.js to behave how we want isn't ideal.

559
00:48:17,486 --> 00:48:20,512
我们不想等待下一个团队来改进单页应用的体验。
We don't want to wait for the next team to make the single page app experience better.

560
00:48:20,750 --> 00:48:23,748
所以我们想转向一个拥有更好单页应用体验的东西。
So we want to move to something that has a better single page app experience.

561
00:48:24,032 --> 00:48:32,452
我们仍希望保持前端和后端部署在一起的连贯性。因此，一个能让我们通过同一个 package.json 把两者结合起来的框架对我们非常有吸引力。
We still want to maintain the cohesion of the front end back end deploying together. So a framework that allows us to have one package JSON that pulls the two together is very enticing to us.

562
00:48:32,974 --> 00:48:35,364
而且我们非常喜欢 Tanner 的构建方式。
And we really like Tanner in the way that he builds.

563
00:48:35,726 --> 00:48:39,748
我们发现 TanStack Start 在很大程度上能满足我们的需求，足够灵活。
We have found TanSec Dart to be, for the most part, flexible enough for our use case.

564
00:48:40,110 --> 00:48:42,912
它还处于非常早期阶段，这让我感到非常不安。
It is still very early, which scares the shit out of me.

565
00:48:43,054 --> 00:48:49,572
而且我们遇到的很多问题，都是因为我们冲进火坑里去为其他人找出解决方案。
And a lot of the problems that we've had are us going headfirst into the fire and bringing out the solutions for everybody else.

566
00:48:49,872 --> 00:48:56,672
比如不得不把所有路由从 TanStack 迁移到 Nitro，这种事情原本会让我根本不想做出这次迁移。
Like having to move all of our routes off of TanStack to Nitro is the type of thing that would have kept me from making the move in the first place.

567
00:48:56,752 --> 00:49:00,612
如果有人告诉我必须得这么做，我就会阻止转向 Tanstack start。
If I was told that that's something we'd have to do, I would have blocked the Tanstack start move.

568
00:49:01,102 --> 00:49:02,032
但现在既然已经
But now that it's

569
00:49:02,032 --> 00:49:04,836
完成了，我们拥有了一个更易于理解的代码库。
done, we have a code base that we understand much better.

570
00:49:05,262 --> 00:49:10,432
之前处理的很多关于离线状态等问题的 Bug，现在变得更加清晰且更容易找到。
A lot of the bugs we were dealing with before around off-state stuff are much clearer and easier for us to find.

571
00:49:10,670 --> 00:49:19,908
我们可以抛弃 Next.js 中那些繁琐的向后兼容和单体式混乱，转而使用一个更简洁、更新、且能更好地满足我们需求的工具。
We get to leave behind all the backwards compat and monolithic chaos that was Next.js with something that's quite a bit more minimal and newer and a little bit more flexible for the things we need.

572
00:49:20,112 --> 00:49:22,352
我们非常喜欢 TanStack Router 的新路由功能。
We love the new routing stuff in Tanstack Router.

573
00:49:22,574 --> 00:49:23,684
它好得多。
It's significantly better.

574
00:49:23,918 --> 00:49:29,860
而且现在，真正每天运营这个项目的团队成员才是负责实现细节的人，而不是我。
And now my team, the people who actually run this every day, are the ones who own the implementation details, not me.

575
00:49:30,286 --> 00:49:35,952
这可以说是最大的收获：代码不再是“由团队来修复 Theo 写出的代码”。
That's arguably the biggest win here is that the code is no longer Theo's code being fixed by the team.

576
00:49:36,174 --> 00:49:37,952
现在，这些代码属于整个团队。
The code is now the team's code.

577
00:49:38,254 --> 00:49:43,552
Mark 和 朱利叶斯 为这些变动付出了巨大的努力。尤其是 朱利叶斯，他为了搞定这一切简直拼了命。
Mark and Julius worked really hard on these changes. Julius in particular went crazy pulling this all off.

578
00:49:43,758 --> 00:49:45,444
我现在可以把手洗干净了。
I get to wipe my hands clean now.

579
00:49:45,646 --> 00:49:46,352
我退出了。
I'm out.

580
00:49:46,670 --> 00:49:50,272
这并不是像你们很多人可能会贴标签那样，仅仅是“转向 TanStack”。
This isn't moving next to Tanstack, as many of you guys are going to brand it.

581
00:49:50,446 --> 00:49:54,628
也不是因为 Theo 对什么新玩意儿感到兴奋。事实上，我甚至可能根本不会选择 TanStack。
This isn't Theo getting excited about the shiny new thing. In fact, I probably wouldn't have even chosen Tanstack.

582
00:49:55,072 --> 00:50:03,952
这是从我为了让 Next.js 按我的意愿运行而堆砌的一堆权宜之计，转向一个团队更熟悉、
This is the move away from Theo's hacky pile of solutions, forcing Next.js to behave how I wanted towards something that the team better understands

583
00:50:04,032 --> 00:50:08,228
且能更好地掌控、并让我们更接近 T3 chat 长期愿景的方案。
and controls that gets us closer to our long-term vision of how we want T3 chat.

584
00:50:08,512 --> 00:50:15,012
我们用一套权宜之计换成了另一套，用一个框架换成了另一个，但到头来，代码库中大部分的代码并没有改变。
We traded one set of hacks for another, we traded one framework for another, but in the end, the majority of the code in the repo didn't change.

585
00:50:15,342 --> 00:50:20,004
我们依然在深耕其中，努力提供最好的聊天体验。
We are still deep in it, trying to make the best possible chat experience.

586
00:50:20,590 --> 00:50:22,192
我的团队现在可以更轻松地进行调试。
My team can now debug more easily.

587
00:50:22,414 --> 00:50:25,188
我们所构建的技术底层感觉整体上更好了一些。
The tech we're building on feels a little better overall.

588
00:50:25,486 --> 00:50:32,612
但说实话，这反而让我更加欣赏 Next.js，以及我之前能够通过各种手段去“压榨”它且大部分情况下都能奏效的事实。
But in the end, this honestly kind of deepened my appreciation for Next and the fact that I could abuse it the ways I did, and it worked for the most part.

589
00:50:32,942 --> 00:50:34,592
而且，真的，伙计。
It also, like, man.

590
00:50:35,552 --> 00:50:44,516
我们在 TanStack 中遇到的扩展性问题和大型代码库规模问题，比如 Nitro 相关的东西，这只是说明了这些技术还处于早期阶段。
The scaling and large code base size issues we've been hitting with Tan Stack, like the Nitro stuff, just it shows how early these things are.

591
00:50:45,070 --> 00:50:46,468
它们确实还很初级。
And they really are.

592
00:50:46,894 --> 00:50:52,452
如果你是来寻求关于下一个项目该用什么技术栈的建议，我没话可说。
If you're here looking for advice on what stack to build your next project with, I got nothing for you.

593
00:50:52,974 --> 00:50:57,700
我在这些技术栈中遇到的问题已经足够多，以至于没有简单、明确的推荐。
I've had enough problems with all of these stacks that there's no easy, obvious recommendation.

594
00:50:58,158 --> 00:50:58,628
是的。
Yeah.

595
00:50:59,054 --> 00:51:03,632
除了内部机制很有趣之外，这并没有什么真正值得借鉴的教训。
There's no real lesson to take from this other than the inner workings are interesting.

596
00:51:03,950 --> 00:51:13,152
一旦你的产品达到一定的规模和体量，在现实世界中，团队及其需求的重要性远超任何框架所能提供的承诺。
And once you ship at a certain size and scale, your team and their needs are way more important in the real world than any particular framework will tell you.

597
00:51:13,454 --> 00:51:20,164
如果有人认为我们的问题可以通过简单切换到 Laravel、或者切换到 TanStack Start 或其他东西来解决，
If anybody thinks our problems can be solved with a simple move to Laravel or a simple move to TanStack Start or some other thing,

598
00:51:20,686 --> 00:51:24,388
他们要么是在骗你因为他们根本不懂，要么就是他们有产品要卖给你。
they're either lying to you because they don't know what they're talking about or they have something to sell you.

599
00:51:24,686 --> 00:51:25,540
别相信他们。
Don't trust them.

600
00:51:25,838 --> 00:51:29,764
我在这里不是为了卖任何东西，除了一个非常棒的 AI 聊天应用，你们绝对应该去看看。
I'm not here to sell you anything other than a really good AI chat app that you should definitely check out.

601
00:51:30,254 --> 00:51:38,352
如果你觉得这跟 Vercel 的漏洞或者那边的各种八卦有关，而忽略了我们一直都在 Vercel 上构建这一切的事实
And if you're thinking that this is something to do with like the Vercel exploit or any drama on that side, and you ignored the fact that we have been building all of this on Vercel

602
00:51:38,512 --> 00:51:46,724
那我也无话可说。我希望你开始仔细点听，因为显然这不是我们不喜欢 Vercel。
the whole time, I don't know what to tell you. I hope you start listening a little more closely because obviously this is not us disliking Vercel.

603
00:51:47,356 --> 00:51:53,152
而是因为我们有非常具体的工程需求，而没有任何框架能完美满足这些需求。
This is us having very specific technical requirements that no framework serves properly.

604
00:51:53,358 --> 00:51:58,180
所以我们试图找到一个最适合被我们“魔改”的框架，来提供我们想要的操作体验。
So we're trying to find the one that we can bastardize the best to give us the experience we want to have.

605
00:51:58,830 --> 00:52:07,472
目前看来，TanStack Start 很有可能能达到要求，因为它包含很多非常好的组件，而且我觉得我们能最大程度地影响到它的开发者
Right now, it seems like Tanztech Start probably will get there, both because it has a lot of really good pieces, and I feel like we can influence the developers building it most

606
00:52:07,662 --> 00:52:09,284
来让它达到我们需要的状态。
to get it where we need it to be.

607
00:52:09,774 --> 00:52:14,788
但是老兄，没有任何东西是按我们想要的方式运行的，而这次迁移过程非常折磨人。
But man, nothing works how we want it to, and this has been a hell of a move.

608
00:52:15,152 --> 00:52:21,220
希望下一段视频能讲讲新功能有多让人兴奋，因为现在这些技术上的障碍已经扫清了。
